00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,635
What is a registry?

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,726
A registry is a server that stores images and hands them out:

3
00:00:11,726 --> 00:00:15,806
docker push uploads an image, docker pull downloads it.

4
00:00:15,806 --> 00:00:19,516
It is how an image built on one machine (a laptop,

5
00:00:19,516 --> 00:00:24,636
a CI runner) reaches every other machine (servers, Kubernetes nodes).

6
00:00:24,636 --> 00:00:27,826
Docker Hub is the default registry; GitHub,

7
00:00:27,826 --> 00:00:35,319
GitLab and every cloud run their own; and you can run one yourself, with the official registry image.

8
