58
00:04:15,813 --> 00:04:18,564
What do I need to remember?

59
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:23,868
A name without a registry is a Docker Hub name:

60
00:04:23,868 --> 00:04:27,114
nginx = docker.io/library/nginx.

61
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:34,806
Log in with an access token (--password-stdin in scripts); push only to a namespace you own.

62
00:04:35,367 --> 00:04:37,852
Tags move, digests do not:

63
00:04:37,852 --> 00:04:41,101
pin by digest for reproducibility.

64
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:45,236
How does image naming work?

65
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,953
An image name is an address:

66
00:04:47,953 --> 00:04:50,644
registry / namespace / repository :

67
00:04:50,644 --> 00:04:52,489
tag, optionally @digest.

68
00:04:52,489 --> 00:04:58,102
Every part except the repository has a default, which is why nginx works.

69
00:04:58,102 --> 00:05:03,099
Knowing the parts tells you where docker push will send an image,

70
00:05:03,099 --> 00:05:06,789
and good tags tell everyone which version it is.

